  nonce: 950d  # 950d
  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). STILL REPRODUCES, and this answers the row's own open question (\"verify whether the scanners can run on non-JS content before deciding severity\"). Status unchanged.\n\n- The hardcodes are still there, at new line numbers: http.py 705/721/739/761/779/797/817/835/853 (was 689/705/723/745), graphql.py 201 (was 164).\n- Reach: `_find_source_files` (http.py:648-651) globs only py/js/ts/jsx/tsx/go/rb/java/elm. The dispatch at http.py:1400-1411 sends every non-py/go/rb/java/elm file to `_scan_javascript_file`, so that scanner only ever sees .js/.ts/.jsx/.tsx. graphql.py:343-346 is the same, minus the other languages. NON-JS CONTENT CANNOT REACH IT.\n- The real consequence is TypeScript mislabelled as javascript. Fixture a.ts with `return fetch(\"/api/items\")` gives the node `javascript:a.ts:2-2:GET /api/items:call_site` with discovery_language=javascript, on a .ts path. The id's language slot disagrees with the file's language.\n\nSuggested scope: derive the language from the file suffix (ts/tsx -> typescript), as the analyzer does. The \"strictly gate the scanners\" alternative in the description is already true."  # 950d
